001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6a315b06d585af5fac518baace5458a440d9efae.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 9:52AM MDT until October 25 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is occurring\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of low lying agricultural areas in Rio Grande\nand Alamosa counties is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 947 AM MDT, emergency management reported flooding of low\nlying areas in Rio Grande county and in Alamosa county upstream\nof the city of Alamosa.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.213ba221d7b769dbc77d0a70fed84b33a31dcfd5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.213ba221d7b769dbc77d0a70fed84b33a31dcfd5.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 6:47AM MDT until October 24 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\n.High flows and flooding will continue along the Rio Grande through\nDel Norte.  The river levels will continue to fall but remain in\nminor flood stage this morning.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte,.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande  near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 5.5 feet, Minor Flood. The Del Norte Riverwalk Trail\nfloods.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:17 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 5.6 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:17 AM MDT Saturday was 6.4 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\nthis morning and continue falling to 3.2 feet Wednesday evening.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.6\nfeet on 06/10/1980.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b7706cb96d83e86d90f0fd7cf1c8f6d13428213c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b7706cb96d83e86d90f0fd7cf1c8f6d13428213c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 241758 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Focus for heavier rainfall shifts to the eastern plains today and Sunday. - Some accumulation snow possible across the higher peaks this afternoon through Sunday morning. - Cooler and wetter weather areawide this weekend, with gradual warming and drying for the u","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T17:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 241720 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1120 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-251730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T06:38:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... Critical fire weather conditions are NOT anticipated over the nex